During the [[New Republic Era]], a '''noodle bar''' serving a [[Unidentified noodle dish (Port Borgo)|noodle dish]] was located on the [[asteroid]] [[Borgo Prime]]. The establishment was managed by a [[Unidentified fry cook|fry cook]] and [[Nibsy]], and the clientele included local [[pirate]]s<ref name="SC 102" /> and thugs.<ref name="SC 102 AD">{{SkeletonCrew|Way, Way Out Past the Barrier}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="SCDate">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> the [[Cantina|bar]] was visited by two young off-worlders [[Wim]] and [[Neel]], who paid the [[Frycook|fry cook]] with [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]]. When the [[Chef|cook]] tried to trick the [[Gender|boys]] into overpaying, a skirmish broke out between him, a [[Unidentified greasy creature|greasy patron]], and pirate [[Vane]]. As a distraction, Wim flipped his bowl with [[noodle]]s to flame up the grill so that he and his companion Neel could run off, prompting the fry cook and his clients to give chase.<ref name="SC 102" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The [[Unidentified noodle dish (Port Borgo)|noodle]] [[Cantina|bar]] debuted in "[[Way, Way Out Past the Barrier]]," the second episode of the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'',<ref name="SC 102" /> which aired on [[December 2]], [[2024]].<ref name="Premiere">{{Twitter|StarWars|status/1861409832349172011|[[Star Wars]]|quote=Mark your calendars. 🗓️ On December 2, stream the two-episode series premiere of #SkeletonCrew, only on @DisneyPlus.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/QwMYe}}</ref> Before the premiere of the show, the bar was first pictured in a [[StarWars.com]] article on [[August 10]], [[2024]].<ref name="SW:2024-08-10">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-official-trailer-key-art|text=''Skeleton Crew'' Official Trailer and Key Art Revealed}}</ref>

